From 64976e1f339b8368454c62e5e160b458320c8b3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:32:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wsputil: keep the memchr() result const in
 decode_text_common()

In C23 mode, glibc's const-preserving string functions (the glibc 2.43
headers this was built against have them) make memchr()
on a const buffer return a const pointer, and GCC 15 warns about
assigning it to the unsigned char * in decode_text_common(), which fails
the -Dwerror=true build:

  wsputil.c:191:5: error: assignment discards 'const' qualifier from
  pointer target type [-Werror=discarded-qualifiers]

The pointer is only read, so declare it const.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/wsputil.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/wsputil.c b/src/wsputil.c
index b6f7c90..b3e33f6 100644
--- a/src/wsputil.c
+++ b/src/wsputil.c
@@ -186,7 +186,7 @@ decode_text_common (const unsigned char *pdu,
                     gboolean             filter_sep,
                     unsigned int        *consumed)
 {
-  unsigned char *c;
+  const unsigned char *c;
 
   c = memchr (pdu, '\0', len);
 
-- 
2.53.0

